                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "80e46a5a-7696-36f6-81db-ca506b52e4c8",
                        "entry_id": "b9ec19c3-dfec-3f4b-888a-5d9b97725661",
                        "glosses": [
                            "podstakannik, tea glass holder"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5998888f-e73c-4652-ad73-edaf15116109",
                                "sense_id": "80e46a5a-7696-36f6-81db-ca506b52e4c8",
                                "text": "[…] Пётр Серге́евич пил свой вече́рний чай. Он подноси́л к губа́м аккура́тно обмо́танный ва́фельным полоте́нцем стака́н, дул в него́ и гро́мко чмо́кал губа́ми.[…]\n—[…] Ты посмотри́, что де́лается. Ло́жек уже́ нет, привы́кли. Ла́дно. А тепе́рь подстака́нники. Где подстака́нники, а? Скажи́ мне, где подстака́нники?\"",
                                "translation": "[…] Pyotr Sergeyevich was drinking his evening tea. He raised the glass, carefully wrapped in a waffle towel, to his lips, blew on it, and loudly smacked his lips. […]\n\" […] Look at what's going on. There's no more spoons, we got used to it. Fine. But now it's the glass-holders. Where are the glass-holders, eh? Tell me, where are the glass-holders?\"",
                                "english": "[…] Pyotr Sergeyevich was drinking his evening tea. He raised the glass, carefully wrapped in a waffle towel, to his lips, blew on it, and loudly smacked his lips. […]\n\" […] Look at what's going on. There's no more spoons, we got used to it. Fine. But now it's the glass-holders. Where are the glass-holders, eh? Tell me, where are the glass-holders?\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
